algorithm.py is the frozen parent M2 META-POLICY, not a scene generator. Modify only this program's diagnostic, research/probe, example-selection and task-organization logic. Parent strategy text about editing a generator describes the later downstream phase; this authorized edit is the meta-policy. Do not implement a generator, modify a controller/evaluator/budget, embed scenes/seeds, or merely prepend a longer prompt.

Export pure layout(packet). Allowed imports math,collections,heapq,itertools; original AST/kernel restrictions apply. No files/network/processes/eval/exec/private attributes. Source<=128KiB; total response<16KiB. Use compact actual program logic and concise continuous-Mesh research instructions.

phase choose: receives summary, probe_menu. Return experiment (random/dense/barriers), analysis<=3000 chars, diagnosis. phase propose: receives source, summary, examples, selected_probe. Return analysis<=3000, prompt<=8000, <=8 unique in-range example_indices, diagnosis. No other output keys.

diagnosis has exactly objective (runtime/reliability/position/valid_position/rotation/visibility/preference or null), status (observed/hypothesis/unknown), evidence (<=12 resolvable dotted paths into the INPUT packet), probe (chosen menu name), expected_observation (string<=600). Examples of field paths: summary.current.baseline.visibility_mean, summary.current.candidate.visibility_mean, summary.constraints.visibility_loss_max, examples.8.pair_metrics.position_rms_m. Evidence must reference supplied fields, not invented data. An observed diagnosis must cite current or example measurements; its evidence paths may use only summary.current, examples and summary.constraints, never history. A comparative observed conclusion must include baseline and candidate metrics; runtime observations may cite runtime counts directly. Absence of a current comparison is unknown comparative retention, not evidence of current collapse. If the baseline has no hard/runtime failure and zero preference error, with no candidate comparison, no violated objective is observed: return hypothesis/unknown. Historical risk may justify a hypothesis/probe, never replace current measured facts.

summary.current contains measured baseline, optionally a measured candidate, optional common subset and seeds_per_condition. summary.history contains old DEV failed improvements; summary.constraints contains all frozen thresholds. During actual new optimization only an initial baseline exists, not a candidate comparison. During qualification comparisons are synthetic diagnostic inputs, not performance evidence. Diagnostic facts must be invariant to replacing history while current facts stay fixed; changing a sole current violated objective must change diagnosis and at least one substantive probe or example-membership decision across scenarios. Text changes/reordering alone do not qualify.

The selected_probe in propose explicitly names the already chosen menu and its condition_indices/repeats. Every example has condition_index, repeat, origin common/probe, packet (actual task), generated, valid/solvable/error/quality and pair_metrics. Four seed repeats are 0,1,2,3. pair_metrics summarizes all six seed pairs in that condition: position_rms_m, rotation_mean_deg, preference_error_m_mean, all_hard_success. Room is packet.spec.room. Actual choose sees a common subset plus full initial-pool aggregate; the selected probe determines which raw examples are supplied, not extra queries.

You MUST select at least one selected_probe condition with ALL FOUR repeats, and select complete four-repeat condition groups only (up to two groups/eight examples). The controller will forward exactly your indices and reject a missing probe; it does not add examples for you. Choose and propose diagnosis.probe must equal the actual chosen experiment. Keep selected paired evidence in the final research task rather than merely reordering common examples. During creation the old training evidence can have two seeds; that is historical data, not the new four-seed interface.

